{
  "description": "Visual check (checks/e2e/w3-visual.e2e.ts). Each turn branches on a tag in its prompt: [LINKS] a reply with a vault wikilink ([[Fixture Note]]), a file link to src/main.ts line 3, a 'C:javascript:' link the link gate must refuse and an https link; [OPTIONS] a numbered-options reply ending in a question; [QUESTION] a reply ending in '?'; [BUSY] a turn that runs a 4 s tool, reading waiting messages at its boundary (press Update meanwhile: it steers in); anything else answers 'Done.' at once, which leaves a completion behind for the toast checks.",
  "autoBackground": true,
  "steps": [
    {
      "repeat": [
        {
          "await": {
            "type": "user"
          },
          "as": "p",
          "timeoutMs": 3600000
        },
        {
          "init": {}
        },
        {
          "if": {
            "saved": "p",
            "contains": "[LINKS]"
          },
          "then": [
            {
              "text": "Here are the links for the check.\n\n- The fixture note: [[Fixture Note]]\n- A file at a line: [main.ts line 3](src/main.ts#L3)\n- A link the gate must refuse: [do not open](C:javascript:alert(1))\n- A web page: [Example](https://example.com/)\n\nThat is all of them."
            },
            {
              "result": "done"
            }
          ],
          "else": [
            {
              "if": {
                "saved": "p",
                "contains": "[OPTIONS]"
              },
              "then": [
                {
                  "text": "There are three ways to do this:\n\n1. Patch the reader in place.\n2. Rewrite the reader behind a flag.\n3. Leave it and document the limit.\n\nWhich option should I take?"
                },
                {
                  "result": "done"
                }
              ],
              "else": [
                {
                  "if": {
                    "saved": "p",
                    "contains": "[QUESTION]"
                  },
                  "then": [
                    {
                      "text": "I finished the first pass and the tests are green. Shall I carry on with the second pass?"
                    },
                    {
                      "result": "done"
                    }
                  ],
                  "else": [
                    {
                      "if": {
                        "saved": "p",
                        "contains": "[BUSY]"
                      },
                      "then": [
                        {
                          "text": "Working on it: first I list the folder."
                        },
                        {
                          "tool": {
                            "id": "tu_busy_{{p.uuid}}",
                            "name": "Bash",
                            "input": {
                              "command": "ls"
                            }
                          }
                        },
                        {
                          "sleep": 4000
                        },
                        {
                          "read": true
                        },
                        {
                          "toolResult": {
                            "id": "tu_busy_{{p.uuid}}",
                            "text": "README.md\nsrc\n"
                          }
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "The folder has a README and a src folder."
                        },
                        {
                          "result": "done"
                        }
                      ],
                      "else": [
                        {
                          "text": "Done. Nothing else to report."
                        },
                        {
                          "result": "done"
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
